{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "pgrad_l97_u_duo_g2_interior",
    "description": "Per-cell operator for pgrad_l97_u_duo_g2 as a match-less named stencil (body = aggregate over the tile/x/y loop indices gt/gi/gj, indexing prognostics relative to those loop vars with the +3 donor-cube halo offset). The rule pgrad_l97_u_duo_g2 is a thin makearray wrapper that applies this once. Original: Pressure-gradient tendency for the covariant u-wind, duo SWE core, Ng=2. L97 four-corner geometric pressure-gradient (Lin 1997) plus the LMARS viscous term, the Zenodo sw_full DEFAULT (Eqs 20-26; akap=1, ptop=0 for SW so pk=pe, gz=Phi_s+Pi and the four-corner du_hydro reduces to the geometric -dx(avg(Phi_s+Pi))/Dx, with the viscous du_pp = rdx/dp*(Pibar_i*Pivis_i - Pibar_i+1*Pivis_i+1)). Pibar = 1/2(dpe+dpw) is the symmetric M**vm face average of the depth pressure (= 1/2 of the two reconstructed interface pressures); Sbar the same for the surface geopotential Phi_s (problem-supplied, 0 for no topography); Pivis = a/2(uE-uW) the LMARS viscous pressure; Dx the arc between x-face midpoints. Add to momentum_u_duo_g2 for the full tendency. Method-of-lines spatial RHS (beta=1, no forward-backward).",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "family:finite_volume",
      "grid:duo",
      "op:pgrad_l97_u",
      "order:3",
      "bc:duo",
      "axes:tile,x,y",
      "form:vector_invariant",
      "esd:stencil"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Chen, X. (2021). The LMARS based shallow-water dynamical core on generic gnomonic cubed-sphere geometry. JAMES 13(1), e2020MS002280.",
        "doi": "10.1029/2020MS002280"
      }
    ]
  },
